import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];OUT=ROOT/'out/rmuc2027-core-native-shapes';views=json.loads((OUT/'compound-renders.json').read_text())
html='''<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{font:14px var(--font-sans);color:var(--foreground)}p{line-height:1.5}nav{display:flex;gap:10px;margin:12px 0}select{font:inherit;padding:8px;background:var(--secondary);color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}img{width:100%;display:block}small{color:var(--muted-foreground)}@media(max-width:480px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style></head><body><p><b>Joint collision · three fitted cylinders</b><br>3,187 source triangles → 3 native primitive descriptions.</p><nav><select id="subject"><option value="joint">Joint housing</option><option value="arm" selected>Arm context</option></select><select id="view"><option value="oblique">Oblique</option><option value="reverse">Reverse</option></select></nav><div class="grid"><div><b>Installed collision</b><img id="before"></div><div><b>Three-cylinder prototype</b><img id="after"></div></div><p>Main barrel + perpendicular branch + short end collar. Hollow regions are intentionally solid. Small rims protrude up to 2.514 mm beyond the fitted union in source samples; contact/clearance review remains.</p><small>Native parameters are exported in JSON and SDF alongside 65,301 retained mesh triangles per Core. This preview tessellates the cylinders for display only. Matched flat-shaded collision renders; visual assets and installed runtime are unchanged. Simulator loading support is still required.</small><script>const views=DATA;function update(){for(const[stage,id]of [['installed','before'],['compound','after']]){document.getElementById(id).src=views.find(v=>v.stage===stage&&v.key===document.querySelector('#subject').value&&v.view===document.querySelector('#view').value).path}}document.querySelectorAll('select').forEach(e=>e.onchange=update);update();</script></body></html>'''.replace('DATA',json.dumps(views))
(OUT/'gallery.html').write_text(html)
